{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1363480-space-opera","id":1363480,"title":"Space Opera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-26T11:09:04-08:00","id":1363480,"title":"Space Opera","content":"Soo very recently I got back into Battletech, mostly due to a SI (self-insert) story I read where a modern person and fan is brought over there due to an HPG experiment. His presence leads to him creating changes in the Federated Suns / Lyran Commonwealth, changes that make it so the Federated Commonwealth is probably going to rule the Inner Sphere. <br /> <br /> The point is that it turned my mind from fantasy to science fiction once again. Which had the side effect of me thinking once again about using the Storypath System as the rule system for such an idea. <br /> <br /> But it also had me think of how we could turn the Trinity Continuum setting into a full space opera sort of setting. One of the like of say Battletech or Dune or Foundation. There being an element of feudal houses and the game of nobles also would be fun. <br /> <br /> I wanted to post this to see if anyone had any ideas or thoughts or suggestions or opinions or comments on a more space opera feel to the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T12:08:00-08:00","id":1363489,"title":"","content":"It has such potential. Though currently Aeon tries do do everything at once and thus in my opinion wouldn't do a space opera as much justice as if you customized the chronicle for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T16:25:43-08:00","id":1363524,"title":"","content":"One thing I would say is that I am not entirely looking at there being Psions/Psiads. I could see, very much in fact, Talents and Superiors. I could see even adding certain Mesmerist elements when we get that group upon Adventure! coming out. But the space opera I am thinking of right now is a lot less magic psionics then what is present in Aeon. <br /> <br /> Of course that idea could easily change upon my mood changing. Which means come this time next week I could be like &quot;yes, lets have psi be super powerful!!&quot; <br /> <br /> I like the idea of both stellar nations and space empires, including the ancient galactic empire that has ruled for eons. I like the idea of both a setting where FTL travel is fast and those where its a much more slow and ponderous system - maybe through using a number of large ships which carry smaller ships through the stars - or even one where its space gates that allow for travel among the empire. <br /> <br /> I also like there being the trappings of nobility, of Space Lords and Dukes and Counts. I think such nobility adds ambiance to a space opera setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T16:40:02-08:00","id":1363526,"title":"","content":"You can pretty easily expand out from \u00c6on out to space opera, and there's a teased/planned supplement way down the line that goes to do that.<br /> <br /> You can take out psi pretty easily without terribly too much issue, except for it currently being the gateway to interstellar travel. But, pick your personal favorite FTL methods and layer it over. Or, keep Teleporters as a thing that need Leviathan ships, kinda like Navigators from Dune/40k.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T16:45:28-08:00","id":1363528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1363480-space-opera?p=1363526#post1363526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can pretty easily expand out from \u00c6on out to space opera, and there's a teased/planned supplement way down the line that goes to do that.<br /> <br /> You can take out psi pretty easily without terribly too much issue, except for it currently being the gateway to interstellar travel. But, pick your personal favorite FTL methods and layer it over. Or, keep Teleporters as a thing that need Leviathan ships, kinda like Navigators from Dune/40k.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah definitely. In fact I look forward to the time in the future when the game has a sourcebook about Aeon space opera. That said, this thread, was basically me saying &quot;hey, I'm in a space opera mood, anyone else in the same mood, and if so, want to talk about it?&quot; and such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Psi teleporters like Dune, star gates, or hyperdrives are all potentially fun ways to go about space travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T17:19:19-08:00","id":1363536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1363480-space-opera?p=1363528#post1363528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah definitely. In fact I look forward to the time in the future when the game has a sourcebook about Aeon space opera. That said, this thread, was basically me saying &amp;quot;hey, I'm in a space opera mood, anyone else in the same mood, and if so, want to talk about it?&amp;quot; and such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Psi teleporters like Dune, star gates, or hyperdrives are all potentially fun ways to go about space travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, most definitely. I finally watched the last half of The Mandalorian earlier this week, and that got the gears turning on how you could get to that point with \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> The individual Prometheus Chambers didn't quite do it for me for Space Opera, and just using Psiads, although cool, didn't quite bring the flavor I wanted, so I thought about there being three main types of Chambers that borrowed from the old Psiad rules, plus a rare/fabled fourth.<br /> <br /> Body (Biokinetic/Vitakinetic)<br /> Mind (Telepathy/Clairvoyance)<br /> Energy (Psychokinetics/Electrokinetics)<br /> And then Exotic or Weird (Teleporter/Quantakinetic)<br /> <br /> There would be multiples of these Chambers in the possession of multiple orders.<br /> <br /> The one hangup I had was cool emblematic weapons without just copping out and having lightsabers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T13:08:55-08:00","id":1363845,"title":"","content":"I like vestiges of lost out there tech from bygone eras, and that screams Q-Tech I guess. Like thinking back on Outlaw Star, and how they had Caster's as lost tech and even getting Shells to use as Ammo was a difficult venture.<br /> <br /> And the type of Freedom and adversity that would give rise to space bounty hunters is a core concept in my Space Operas. Remember in the same time period we had Cowboy Bebop, Outlaw Star and Trigun. Three very different visions of the future but they had Bounty Hunters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}